WEBVTT

00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:16.240
The target has entered the department 
store at an ordinary but brisk clip.

00:00:19.870 --> 00:00:21.630
<i>I'm here. What now?</i>

00:00:21.630 --> 00:00:24.120
<i>The outside is under police surveillance,</i>

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:26.230
<i>so could you head inside and capture her?</i>

00:00:26.230 --> 00:00:27.320
Okay.

00:00:39.710 --> 00:00:41.520
That's weird.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:44.850
This doesn't seem right, Ysley-kun.

00:00:44.850 --> 00:00:48.860
I looked all over, including underground, 
but I don't see Miku anywhere.

00:00:49.150 --> 00:00:53.360
Either it's some kind of trick,
or she's still hiding somewhere...

00:00:53.360 --> 00:00:56.610
More importantly, 
why is she doing any of this?

00:00:57.660 --> 00:00:59.770
Miku said it herself...

00:01:00.910 --> 00:01:03.890
If the enemy starts wondering
how we managed to escape

00:01:00.910 --> 00:01:08.210
<b>#11
Smells Fishy</b>

00:01:03.890 --> 00:01:07.620
or if there's any point left,
then it's our victory.

00:01:08.230 --> 00:01:11.960
That bitch is pretty smart after all.

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:25.030
<b><i>The Idaten Deities
</i>\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hKnow Only Peace</b>

00:02:41.010 --> 00:02:42.010
<b><i>The Idaten Deities
</i>\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hKnow Only Peace</b>

00:02:50.390 --> 00:02:54.870
I'm not seeing that creature... 
Where could it have gone?

00:03:07.190 --> 00:03:11.670
You've got plenty of speed,
but you're still sorely lacking in power!

00:03:15.460 --> 00:03:17.920
Paula! Get back!

00:03:17.920 --> 00:03:19.670
You demon!

00:03:24.580 --> 00:03:26.390
Ow, ow, ow, ow, ow, ow!

00:03:26.660 --> 00:03:28.890
R-Rin-san...

00:03:28.890 --> 00:03:35.060
Cory-kun is on our side, 
so you can't... kill... him...

00:03:37.230 --> 00:03:38.310
P-Paula-chan!

00:03:38.310 --> 00:03:40.090
Hang in there! Are you okay?

00:03:41.090 --> 00:03:42.200
Yeah...

00:03:42.200 --> 00:03:45.190
I'll probably heal... sooner or later?

00:03:45.190 --> 00:03:47.620
I'm not... too sure...

00:03:47.620 --> 00:03:52.390
Just hold the wound closed. 
She'll heal soon enough.

00:03:52.390 --> 00:03:54.120
L-Like this?

00:03:54.110 --> 00:03:58.640
What exactly are you? Are you a demon?

00:03:58.640 --> 00:04:00.760
Uh... well...

00:04:02.950 --> 00:04:03.840
Oh?

00:04:03.840 --> 00:04:05.400
Hey, it's the old bat.

00:04:05.400 --> 00:04:08.350
What the hell? You finally feeling better?

00:04:08.350 --> 00:04:11.740
And Paula's all torn to shit... 
What's new, though?

00:04:13.320 --> 00:04:16.730
<i>That creature that resembled a demon
 and appeared from nowhere...</i>

00:04:16.730 --> 00:04:18.990
<i>And this one who's clearly a demon,</i>

00:04:18.990 --> 00:04:22.410
<i>yet is concerned about Paula
and supposedly an ally...</i>

00:04:22.990 --> 00:04:27.870
<i>Then there's that old man who has
 my grandfather and his friends' memories...</i>

00:04:28.150 --> 00:04:31.130
<i>What in the world is going on?</i>

00:04:32.740 --> 00:04:34.710
What's with all the cops?

00:04:34.710 --> 00:04:37.670
Something about a violent 
criminal being in there.

00:04:37.670 --> 00:04:39.780
I heard some people have been
 killed inside, too.

00:04:39.780 --> 00:04:41.360
Oh, my. How dreadful.

00:04:42.210 --> 00:04:44.840
Looks like the experiment's a success...

00:04:45.260 --> 00:04:45.970
Hayato!

00:04:46.620 --> 00:04:47.940
What is it, you old hag?

00:04:47.940 --> 00:04:50.080
What in the world is going on?

00:04:50.080 --> 00:04:51.610
I demand an explanation!

00:04:52.020 --> 00:04:52.730
From me?

00:04:55.140 --> 00:04:59.020
Say, Cory-kun, could you not squeeze those?

00:04:59.020 --> 00:05:01.410
Huh? U-Uh... I, um...

00:05:01.410 --> 00:05:02.840
S-Sorry.

00:05:02.840 --> 00:05:05.150
It's kind of making my wound hurt.

00:05:05.150 --> 00:05:06.780
Wait, that's why?

00:05:06.780 --> 00:05:10.210
You wanna know exactly what's going on, huh?

00:05:10.210 --> 00:05:12.660
Well, do you remember how we invaded 
demon central a while back?

00:05:16.650 --> 00:05:20.550
So... Ysley and Prontea are looking 
for the demons who escaped,

00:05:20.550 --> 00:05:21.670
and that about covers it.

00:05:22.350 --> 00:05:24.410
<i>He actually did a decent job?!</i>

00:05:24.410 --> 00:05:27.930
Is that all? Then I've got another question.

00:05:27.930 --> 00:05:31.550
There was a man in that fight
who had my grandfather's memories.

00:05:31.550 --> 00:05:33.810
How is such a thing possible?

00:05:34.960 --> 00:05:36.190
What're you talking about?

00:05:37.080 --> 00:05:37.940
Not good...

00:05:38.480 --> 00:05:42.810
General Piscalat, could you shut down all 
of the surveillance equipment on the island

00:05:42.810 --> 00:05:44.410
where Hayato and the others are?

00:05:45.190 --> 00:05:48.160
<i>If there's any data of this on the computers,
 the Demon Lord might find it.</i>

00:05:48.580 --> 00:05:51.950
<i>We don't want Rin's past coming to light.</i>

00:05:51.950 --> 00:05:54.350
<i>Granted, I doubt he'd
 be able to figure that out</i>

00:05:54.350 --> 00:05:58.740
<i>that he's an Idaten from inside 
the seal just based on that, but...</i>

00:05:59.760 --> 00:06:04.210
<i>Miku's a different story. She might only
need the vaguest hint at this point.</i>

00:06:04.210 --> 00:06:07.240
<i>This conversation might end up
 divulging a ton of intel.</i>

00:06:07.240 --> 00:06:09.590
<i>Maybe we should recall Cory-kun soon...</i>

00:06:09.590 --> 00:06:12.220
<i>I'll poke around his brain
 and erase anything problematic.</i>

00:06:14.970 --> 00:06:18.730
Ideally we'd get two... 
but one should be enough.

00:06:18.730 --> 00:06:21.260
As for the timing, let's see...

00:06:21.730 --> 00:06:24.730
<i>Once Cory comes back to Zoble, I think.</i>

00:06:24.980 --> 00:06:26.830
From what you've seen,

00:06:26.830 --> 00:06:29.990
this Idaten is the only one with
 a knack for actual strategy, right?

00:06:29.990 --> 00:06:34.740
That's right. I'd say that the rest are 
probably of lower than average intelligence.

00:06:34.740 --> 00:06:38.380
Which means, bare minimum, 
we need to kill him...

00:06:39.520 --> 00:06:44.060
Because brute strength will 
never help them find me.

00:06:45.060 --> 00:06:58.960
Mandate! Mandate!

00:06:45.720 --> 00:06:47.870
It oughta be mandatory to support women!

00:06:46.800 --> 00:06:52.050
Bring back our support!!!

00:06:46.800 --> 00:06:52.050
No Line Work!!

00:06:46.800 --> 00:06:52.050
Let's make a living with sex alone!

00:06:46.800 --> 00:06:52.050
Who are the real slaves?!

00:06:47.870 --> 00:06:50.380
You think we can work regular jobs
 after what's happened?!

00:06:50.380 --> 00:06:54.180
Rich guys should have to support
 a thousand women apiece!

00:06:54.180 --> 00:06:56.020
What's going on with that protest?

00:06:56.020 --> 00:06:58.960
Miku's reeducation was so effective on them,

00:06:58.960 --> 00:07:00.940
they're rejecting any other kind of work.

00:07:01.820 --> 00:07:04.680
It's like everything she touches
 turns into a problem.

00:07:04.680 --> 00:07:07.440
Why don't you head to bed, General Piscalat?

00:07:07.740 --> 00:07:10.000
I appreciate your concern,

00:07:10.530 --> 00:07:13.700
but after working with you over these 
years and never seeing you rest,

00:07:13.700 --> 00:07:17.210
the idea of taking time for 
myself is a bit disheartening.

00:07:17.750 --> 00:07:20.680
Considering our physiological differences, 
that's just the way it is.

00:07:20.680 --> 00:07:21.710
I'll see you later, okay?

00:07:21.710 --> 00:07:25.060
Yes... In that case, 
maybe I'll take your suggestion.

00:07:26.960 --> 00:07:28.610
<i>He's pretty incredible...</i>

00:07:28.610 --> 00:07:32.300
<i>being able to work effectively
 without ever resting.</i>

00:07:32.300 --> 00:07:33.870
<i>And unlike every other man I've worked with,</i>

00:07:33.870 --> 00:07:36.970
<i>we've been alone for long periods of time
 and he's never tried anything.</i>

00:07:37.770 --> 00:07:39.910
<i>I almost wish he would...</i>

00:07:41.330 --> 00:07:44.610
<i>Wait, no, no! What am I thinking?!</i>

00:07:44.610 --> 00:07:46.880
Is something wrong, General Piscalat?

00:07:47.850 --> 00:07:49.690
Wh-What is it?

00:07:50.500 --> 00:07:51.240
Shut up!

00:07:51.240 --> 00:07:52.650
I'm just tired!

00:07:52.650 --> 00:07:54.820
That's right! It's just exhaustion!

00:07:54.820 --> 00:07:55.950
That has to be it!

00:07:55.950 --> 00:07:58.300
I'm going to get a few hours' rest.

00:07:58.300 --> 00:08:00.220
Interrupt and you're in for an execution!

00:08:00.220 --> 00:08:03.330
R-Right... Rest well, ma'am.

00:08:03.330 --> 00:08:06.840
<b>Shower Room</b>

00:08:03.330 --> 00:08:06.840
<b>Stay out!</b>

00:08:07.930 --> 00:08:10.840
I think maybe now's a good time...

00:08:13.470 --> 00:08:15.230
If we're not certain what the enemy is up to,

00:08:15.230 --> 00:08:18.180
then for now, we'll have to simply get 
strong enough to erase any doubts!

00:08:22.290 --> 00:08:26.150
<i>Ugh... she's just gone back to her old self.</i>

00:08:26.390 --> 00:08:31.400
Do I really need to stick around if the 
monster lady is back in the equation?

00:08:33.280 --> 00:08:35.710
Hey, speak of the devil. 
There's my recall order.

00:08:37.530 --> 00:08:40.540
Paula-chan, there's no real 
point in me sticking around,

00:08:40.540 --> 00:08:41.960
so I'm heading back to Zoble.

00:08:42.600 --> 00:08:45.670
Okay. Have a safe trip.

00:08:45.670 --> 00:08:50.670
They want me to bring you along.
 Didn't say why.

00:08:50.670 --> 00:08:53.000
Really? I'll go.

00:08:53.000 --> 00:08:55.930
And then hopefully I won't 
have to come back...

00:09:01.060 --> 00:09:03.460
Is the ventilation busted?

00:09:03.460 --> 00:09:05.230
The steam isn't dissipating at all.

00:09:05.530 --> 00:09:08.690
I'll have the idiot who's 
responsible executed later.

00:09:09.040 --> 00:09:10.330
Damn it all...

00:09:14.120 --> 00:09:15.950
Th-This is...

00:09:16.870 --> 00:09:19.380
<i>It's... the same drug... from before...</i>

00:09:20.370 --> 00:09:22.240
<i>B-But who?</i>

00:09:28.380 --> 00:09:30.220
<i>Impossible... How?</i>

00:09:30.220 --> 00:09:32.380
<i>I should be the only one 
who can get in here.</i>

00:09:33.660 --> 00:09:38.640
Yeah, these chemicals definitely seem to 
have an immediate effect on human brains.

00:09:38.990 --> 00:09:41.900
<i>A regular soldier? How?!</i>

00:09:42.380 --> 00:09:45.640
Y-You wretch... D-Don't think you'll...

00:09:47.160 --> 00:09:48.130
Don't look...

00:09:49.380 --> 00:09:51.540
It's nothing to be embarrassed about,
 Piscalat, my dear.

00:09:51.540 --> 00:09:54.900
I've already seen you in the nude 
during your physicals, haven't I?

00:09:54.900 --> 00:09:58.160
I-Is that you... Your Lordship?

00:09:59.920 --> 00:10:02.270
Mechanical bodies are quite convenient.

00:10:02.270 --> 00:10:04.280
They let you impersonate whoever you want.

00:10:10.870 --> 00:10:15.550
The demon sightings have all been 
in the radius of this area...

00:10:16.310 --> 00:10:18.430
And General Piscalat is late.

00:10:18.430 --> 00:10:20.730
Maybe she's actually getting
 some decent sleep for once.

00:10:25.430 --> 00:10:27.070
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:10:27.070 --> 00:10:31.190
I was wondering... 
where is Prontea-san right now?

00:10:31.190 --> 00:10:35.020
Prontea-san? Right now he should be 
in the vicinity of the Gaina Coast

00:10:35.020 --> 00:10:36.610
looking for Raki and Kroft—

00:10:37.550 --> 00:10:42.450
I see. That's all I need to know,
 you piece of shit!

00:10:46.940 --> 00:10:49.600
Don't worry. You won't die just yet.

00:10:49.600 --> 00:10:53.340
I wouldn't be satisfied
 letting you off that easy.

00:10:53.340 --> 00:10:56.500
Oh, dear... Was it something 
I said, Piscalat-chan?

00:10:56.500 --> 00:10:59.470
<i>This is bad. Her brainwashing's 
been completely undone.</i>

00:11:00.470 --> 00:11:04.110
What's wrong? Did you 
implant a bomb in my body?

00:11:04.110 --> 00:11:07.970
You think you're gonna blow the place? 
Or make an emergency call to Prontea?

00:11:07.970 --> 00:11:10.480
Too bad you can't do any of that

00:11:10.480 --> 00:11:12.730
if the gizmos you hide 
in your body won't work.

00:11:12.730 --> 00:11:15.480
<i>How? Why aren't they working?</i>

00:11:15.740 --> 00:11:20.740
You see, when all electrical devices are 
disabled, you can't use any of them.

00:11:21.020 --> 00:11:22.100
Pete?

00:11:22.100 --> 00:11:23.240
No... the Demon Lord!

00:11:23.460 --> 00:11:26.370
I see. So that was you.

00:11:26.370 --> 00:11:28.500
You switched faces and clothing at the store—

00:11:28.500 --> 00:11:29.710
Correct you are.

00:11:29.710 --> 00:11:34.000
And if you had caught on sooner, 
this entire plan would have been scrapped.

00:11:35.760 --> 00:11:38.400
Looks like the Demon Lord's 
pulled it off, Merku.

00:11:38.400 --> 00:11:43.760
I see. Does that mean my skin-suit crafting 
life has finally come to an end?

00:11:43.760 --> 00:11:45.270
Granted...

00:11:45.270 --> 00:11:50.310
I thought I was done for when 
he peeked in on the changing room.

00:11:50.310 --> 00:11:54.340
<i>That implies one of the customers 
reacted to Prontea-san searching...</i>

00:11:54.340 --> 00:11:57.520
<i>How could he have not noticed that?! Damn it!</i>

00:12:02.490 --> 00:12:04.530
I see you're both back.

00:12:05.250 --> 00:12:09.230
Let's get to business, Paula. 
You're to join Ysley-dono.

00:12:09.230 --> 00:12:12.500
Cory, you were recalled
 because your job on the island is done.

00:12:12.500 --> 00:12:14.750
Why not grab something to eat?

00:12:15.010 --> 00:12:19.960
Piscalat-neechan said there wouldn't
be any missions any time soon,

00:12:19.960 --> 00:12:24.130
but I'm betting I'll be sent to help 
Prontea-san hunt wild demons—

00:12:24.840 --> 00:12:28.850
H-Huh? I'm getting... sleepy...

00:12:33.770 --> 00:12:36.220
I appreciate how straightforward
 you are, Cory.

00:12:36.220 --> 00:12:39.320
Being asleep will make 
the procedure a lot smoother.

00:12:39.990 --> 00:12:41.570
Paula!

00:12:42.410 --> 00:12:47.070
Where did she go? There's no sign
 of her coming back, either.

00:12:47.070 --> 00:12:50.330
Maybe you kicked her ass too hard this time.

00:12:50.330 --> 00:12:54.130
I have to agree that Rin-san's training 
can be a bit overly severe at times.

00:12:54.130 --> 00:12:54.580
Yep.

00:12:54.580 --> 00:12:58.200
She seems to have headed 
to Zoble along with Cory-san...

00:12:58.200 --> 00:12:59.840
I'll ask about it.

00:13:04.090 --> 00:13:07.410
You've mastered those human tools, then?!

00:13:07.410 --> 00:13:10.840
So you're one of those 
egghead types like Ysley?!

00:13:10.840 --> 00:13:14.100
What are you talking about?
 It's just a cell phone.

00:13:14.100 --> 00:13:16.100
But... Huh? No answer.

00:13:16.100 --> 00:13:17.610
Is that you, Gill-chan?

00:13:17.610 --> 00:13:20.320
It's sure rare for you to dial me up!

00:13:20.320 --> 00:13:21.190
Paula?

00:13:21.190 --> 00:13:22.920
You're wondering where she is?

00:13:22.920 --> 00:13:26.530
I haven't heard, actually.
 You're better off asking Ysley-kun...

00:13:26.530 --> 00:13:27.490
Wait, what?

00:13:34.930 --> 00:13:38.830
We should never lose communications
with the command center!

00:13:39.580 --> 00:13:41.650
Ysley-kun! General Piscalat!

00:13:42.090 --> 00:13:43.050
Damn it...

00:13:43.050 --> 00:13:46.590
<i>They got us!
 But who actually attacked and how?</i>

00:13:46.590 --> 00:13:50.850
<i>I can't imagine Ysley-kun and General Piscalat
 losing if they were together.</i>

00:13:50.850 --> 00:13:53.560
<i>And even against an overwhelming opponent,</i>

00:13:53.560 --> 00:13:57.210
<i>I think he'd probably abandon her to flee.</i>

00:14:03.280 --> 00:14:05.880
I'd say we finished up in the nick of time.

00:14:06.320 --> 00:14:07.700
Say, Your Lordship,

00:14:07.700 --> 00:14:11.410
what would you have done if undoing
my brainwashing had taken another 30 minutes?

00:14:11.410 --> 00:14:13.290
Die, most likely.

00:14:15.540 --> 00:14:18.330
Damn it... They really got us!

00:14:18.970 --> 00:14:21.920
Should I be more angry or worried?

00:14:23.770 --> 00:14:24.920
Who is it?! What do you want?!

00:14:24.920 --> 00:14:30.140
What's all this? I couldn't 
get in touch with Piscalat or Ysley,

00:14:30.140 --> 00:14:32.680
and now I hear command's 
been blown up or something.

00:14:32.680 --> 00:14:34.680
Neput? What are you doing right now?

00:14:34.680 --> 00:14:37.310
Working on the treaties and 
other paperwork to establish

00:14:37.310 --> 00:14:39.090
diplomatic crap with Hotaena and Sarabael.

00:14:39.090 --> 00:14:41.330
That doesn't matter! 
I need you here! Right now!

00:14:41.330 --> 00:14:42.690
No, I'll come to you!

00:14:44.420 --> 00:14:46.280
Has something happened?

00:14:46.280 --> 00:14:49.670
Not sure exactly, but it's probably bad news.

00:14:49.670 --> 00:14:53.410
That damn Miku is always a pain in the 
ass when you get on her bad side.

00:14:53.410 --> 00:14:56.290
I'd say this was basically 
the best possible result.

00:14:56.290 --> 00:15:02.040
We were able to recover Piscalat and Cory, 
and the enemy isn't aware of that yet.

00:15:02.040 --> 00:15:04.540
So, what shall we do next?

00:15:04.540 --> 00:15:06.290
Let's see...

00:15:06.290 --> 00:15:09.590
For now... let's not make any moves.

00:15:09.590 --> 00:15:13.420
Oh, no, not you! You should 
keep moving even harder, okay?

00:15:13.860 --> 00:15:14.510
Yeah...

00:15:14.870 --> 00:15:18.580
We managed to collect two Idaten samples.

00:15:18.580 --> 00:15:23.520
Why not spend some time studying them?
 At a nice, leisurely pace.

00:15:23.520 --> 00:15:25.520
Now then...

00:15:25.520 --> 00:15:27.840
Do you understand what's about to happen?

00:15:27.840 --> 00:15:29.280
How about you, missy?

00:15:30.530 --> 00:15:33.780
I kind of think we might die...

00:15:33.780 --> 00:15:35.650
You think you're gonna die, huh?

00:15:35.650 --> 00:15:38.290
That's a cute answer.

00:15:38.290 --> 00:15:41.770
But for now, the physical exam comes first.

00:15:42.290 --> 00:15:46.640
For example, what's going on in here?!

00:15:47.050 --> 00:15:48.410
<i>Oh, torture.</i>

00:15:48.410 --> 00:15:52.010
<i>Aw, man, this is probably gonna hurt a lot.</i>

00:15:52.010 --> 00:15:55.500
You're gonna learn there are 
things worse than death...

00:15:56.300 --> 00:15:58.010
<i>She's not screaming?</i>

00:15:58.770 --> 00:15:59.500
Ouchie!

00:15:59.500 --> 00:16:01.480
Hey, don't kill her.

00:16:01.720 --> 00:16:03.850
Quit trying to act tough, you little shit.

00:16:03.850 --> 00:16:06.660
Yeowch! Ouch, ouch, ouch...

00:16:05.480 --> 00:16:08.480
<i>Why the hell isn't she 
screaming her head off?</i>

00:16:08.480 --> 00:16:10.870
You're next.

00:16:10.870 --> 00:16:14.110
I don't think a regular rectal 
probe is gonna cut it for you.

00:16:14.110 --> 00:16:18.240
Maybe I'll slice you open 
from your intestines to your throat.

00:16:18.240 --> 00:16:21.500
His mouth, too. Pull all those teeth out.

00:16:21.500 --> 00:16:26.400
No, maybe rip his entire face off
starting with his eyes.

00:16:30.680 --> 00:16:32.280
Those're some sweet sounds you're making!

00:16:33.750 --> 00:16:37.910
Our flesh returns to the earth,
 and our souls to the Lord's side.

00:16:38.210 --> 00:16:41.970
Please look over us, who inherit Your works.

00:16:42.840 --> 00:16:45.380
That concludes the prayer for the dead,

00:16:45.380 --> 00:16:48.520
but was it really all right 
to use rites from my country?

00:16:48.520 --> 00:16:50.900
It's okay, sister.

00:16:51.180 --> 00:16:53.420
The important thing isn't the ritual itself,

00:16:53.420 --> 00:16:56.720
but rather nurturing the belief that 
the dead should be honored.

00:16:57.300 --> 00:17:00.910
I realize I'm not in any position to ask
such a thing from you, but...

00:17:02.150 --> 00:17:06.040
No. This is all I can really do, so...

00:17:06.040 --> 00:17:12.420
Besides, lately, I've begun to question 
what's truly good or evil.

00:17:12.760 --> 00:17:14.800
You think we should make 
peace with the demons?

00:17:14.800 --> 00:17:18.860
I do! If we don't have to fight, 
wouldn't we be better if we didn't?

00:17:18.860 --> 00:17:22.020
They were worried about my well being.

00:17:22.020 --> 00:17:24.300
I'm sure we can come to an 
understanding if we just talk.

00:17:24.300 --> 00:17:25.860
Okay, let's do that.

00:17:26.310 --> 00:17:27.970
But in that case,

00:17:27.970 --> 00:17:30.070
we're going to need thousands of human babies

00:17:30.070 --> 00:17:33.820
in order to maintain the demon population.

00:17:34.480 --> 00:17:35.650
That's...

00:17:35.650 --> 00:17:36.570
Out of the question?

00:17:36.570 --> 00:17:40.120
In that case, the demons will have 
to be prohibited from reproducing

00:17:40.120 --> 00:17:42.080
until they die out from natural causes.

00:17:43.450 --> 00:17:45.780
What you're suggesting in that case
 isn't a compromise.

00:17:45.780 --> 00:17:47.930
It's a one-sided death sentence.

00:17:48.500 --> 00:17:51.580
The only path to peace 
is finding a way for Idaten, humans,

00:17:51.580 --> 00:17:54.190
and demons to all be satisfied.

00:17:56.930 --> 00:17:59.460
Is everybody here, Your Lordship?

00:17:59.460 --> 00:18:00.180
Indeed.

00:18:00.180 --> 00:18:03.720
It's a rundown farm, but there 
are facilities underground.

00:18:03.720 --> 00:18:06.390
We'll conduct the experiments 
on the Idaten here, as well.

00:18:06.390 --> 00:18:09.100
Oh, I'd love to help with that part.

00:18:09.320 --> 00:18:12.880
I've got some pretty personal 
grudges against them.

00:18:16.870 --> 00:18:19.490
Oh, hey, Cory. It's been a while.

00:18:22.000 --> 00:18:23.740
Cory-kun...

00:18:27.210 --> 00:18:29.700
According to the deities, in Zoble,

00:18:29.700 --> 00:18:33.720
the demons were attempting to mass-produce 
humans that they could fuse with demons.

00:18:33.720 --> 00:18:37.450
They were just desperate to ensure 
the survival of their species...

00:18:39.340 --> 00:18:44.220
Maybe I went a little overboard 
for the first day. Can't have her dying.

00:18:44.580 --> 00:18:47.730
Hurry up and heal. 
Then I'll get to cutting again.

00:18:47.730 --> 00:18:52.230
We'll change the type of pain
 over and over again...

00:18:52.230 --> 00:18:55.890
Hey. Sorry, Cory, looks like the 
experiments for today are...

00:18:56.480 --> 00:18:59.220
What's wrong? You look kind of sick.

00:18:59.220 --> 00:19:03.310
Oh, yeah... Probably because my 
brainwashing was just undone.

00:19:03.310 --> 00:19:05.300
Guess I'm kinda tired, you know?

00:19:05.300 --> 00:19:09.000
<i>What is this? The brainwashing was undone...</i>

00:19:10.120 --> 00:19:12.130
Maybe I should get some sleep.

00:19:12.130 --> 00:19:15.130
It hurts... It hurts...

00:19:16.750 --> 00:19:18.670
Well, it's your turn to keep watch.

00:19:18.670 --> 00:19:19.760
You got it.

00:19:21.290 --> 00:19:23.760
<i>So, based on the information 
I got from Piscalat,</i>

00:19:24.110 --> 00:19:26.440
<i>the Demon Lord is practically 
confirmed to be an Idaten</i>

00:19:26.440 --> 00:19:29.790
<i>who came into existence 
on the other side of the seal.</i>

00:19:30.520 --> 00:19:32.120
I'm so bored...

00:19:32.120 --> 00:19:34.520
Could one of you two get pregnant already?

00:19:34.520 --> 00:19:36.400
And what am I supposed to do differently?

00:19:36.400 --> 00:19:39.900
From a human perspective,
it's easy to condemn what they do.

00:19:39.900 --> 00:19:42.910
But as a mere fellow living thing, I can't.

00:19:43.680 --> 00:19:46.620
A way for all of our species to coexist...

00:19:46.950 --> 00:19:49.690
I can't imagine how to get there,

00:19:50.210 --> 00:19:54.360
but... is there really no compromise at all?

00:20:00.080 --> 00:20:03.380
Prontea-san just suggested that Ysley-san

00:20:03.380 --> 00:20:06.630
and Paula-san have been 
captured by the enemy...

00:20:06.630 --> 00:20:07.970
S-Say what?!

00:20:07.970 --> 00:20:09.630
Who got them?!

00:20:09.630 --> 00:20:10.730
I don't know.

00:20:10.870 --> 00:20:12.690
Where do we go to save them?!

00:20:12.690 --> 00:20:13.850
I don't know...

00:20:13.980 --> 00:20:15.840
Are you sure they were taken?

00:20:15.840 --> 00:20:17.730
I... don't know.

00:20:17.730 --> 00:20:22.200
You fool! It seems like 
you don't know anything!

00:20:20.660 --> 00:20:25.530
Please stop! If you break the phone, 
we really won't be able to learn anything!

00:20:25.530 --> 00:20:28.700
Hayato-san! Stop her, please!

00:20:26.990 --> 00:20:28.700
Hey, calm down, Granny.

00:20:28.700 --> 00:20:30.060
Shut it!

00:20:33.000 --> 00:20:35.210
What in the world is happening?

00:20:36.570 --> 00:20:37.850
Rin-san, where are you going?

00:20:37.850 --> 00:20:41.470
Isn't it obvious?! To find Ysley and Paula!

00:20:42.450 --> 00:20:45.180
Does she have any idea 
where to start looking?

00:20:45.590 --> 00:20:47.150
Ysley!

00:20:47.150 --> 00:20:48.500
Paula!

00:20:48.500 --> 00:20:50.720
Where are you?!

00:20:52.850 --> 00:20:55.310
Where are you?!

00:20:57.810 --> 00:21:01.620
Where are you?!

00:21:21.860 --> 00:21:25.050
<b>The Idaten Deities Know Only Peace</b>
